    "b-10-run-director-loop-deterministic-run-schedu-2": {
      "id": "b-10-run-director-loop-deterministic-run-schedu-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The Run Loop is the host controller for board admission, worker-job consumption, settlement, serial integration, and epoch boundaries. Workers perform target-local research and source edits in Daytona sandboxes. The host owns the queue, durable evidence, and canonical harness checkout."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-run-director-loop-the-run-scheduler-is-the-3": {
      "id": "b-10-run-director-loop-the-run-scheduler-is-the-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The loop realizes admitted board targets as deduplicated worker jobs and settles those jobs from closed worker-state evidence. A claim captures the base revision used to provision its sandbox. Knowledge task production and consumption run through separately enabled lanes."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-run-director-loop-behavior-4": {
      "id": "b-10-run-director-loop-behavior-4",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Canonical Loop"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-run-director-loop-text-18": {
      "id": "b-10-run-director-loop-text-18",
      "type": "process-outline",
      "props": {
        "steps": [
          {
            "text": "Run Loop",
            "steps": [
              {
                "text": "Require a schedulable run and its --lease-id. Reconcile sandbox records at startup."
              },
              {
                "text": "Heartbeat dispatch authority, reap expired worker jobs and claims, and settle closed worker states."
              },
              {
                "text": "Admit eligible board candidates at epoch open, refresh availability, and repair missing or orphaned worker-job coverage."
              },
              {
                "text": "Let the hosted consumer atomically claim a worker job and epoch target. Provision its Daytona sandbox at the captured base revision."
              },
              {
                "text": "Drain eligible worker-output integrations in single flight. Commit accepted paths and advance the base for future workers. Preserve blocking outcomes as durable evidence."
              },
              {
                "text": "Wait for active worker and integration work before the epoch boundary. Rebuild report evidence, defer regression findings, reconcile upstream, and run publication gates."
              },
              {
                "text": "Respect boundary pause, retry timing, and retry exhaustion. Close with durable evidence and admit the next epoch only when the boundary permits it."
              },
              {
                "text": "Run configured knowledge maintenance when due and safe. Start summary and librarian consumers only under their respective flags."
              },
              {
                "text": "Handle the selected wake signal, expose scheduler conditions, and wait for settlement, background work, or the idle cadence."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-run-director-loop-the-run-loop-is-the-non-19": {
      "id": "b-10-run-director-loop-the-run-loop-is-the-non-19",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Closed worker states remain durable evidence for successes, non-improvements, and failures. When --worker-summary is enabled, the summary processor catches up ended worker states that lack a summary job and writes structured run knowledge. --librarian-consumer independently enables librarian task consumption. A closed worker does not guarantee either lane is enabled or that a librarian pass has completed."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-run-director-loop-epoch-cycle-21": {
      "id": "b-10-run-director-loop-epoch-cycle-21",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Runtime Capacity Inputs"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-run-director-loop-an-epoch-is-a-bounded-sc-22": {
      "id": "b-10-run-director-loop-an-epoch-is-a-bounded-sc-22",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "At epoch admission, the scheduler reads ranked board candidates and applies the optional --epoch-target-cap. Without a cap it considers the full candidate list. The fresh-report gate is enabled by default and requires the report to match the board provenance hash. Existing epoch membership stays fixed while availability and job coverage are refreshed."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-run-director-loop-concept-purpose-35": {
      "id": "b-10-run-director-loop-concept-purpose-35",
      "type": "structured-table",
      "props": {
        "columns": [
          "Input",
          "Run Loop Action"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "Worker pool size",
            "Cap active worker jobs at min(desiredWorkers, --max-workers)."
          ],
          [
            "Epoch target cap",
            "Limit candidates considered during admission when --epoch-target-cap is supplied."
          ],
          [
            "Sandbox profile",
            "Provision the configured resources per worker claim. Worker compilation and tools run inside that sandbox."
          ],
          [
            "Dispatch and boundary state",
            "Pause claims when authority is blocked or the epoch is paused. Serialize canonical integration and boundary work."
          ]
        ]
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-run-director-loop-wake-events-39": {
